    dcterms:description "Resilient fall classifier. Each candidate fall must survive a multi-step critical event sequence that validates duration AND impact strength before a determination is broadcast to listeners. RED (emergency dispatch) requires six consecutive ticks of progressive evidence: motion onset → sustained motion → severe motion → post-impact stillness onset → sustained stillness → very-sustained stillness. AMBER tiers report less-certain patterns (recovered stumbles, recovered impacts, sustained instability) without escalating to emergency." ;
